  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef calculus_hessian_convexity(X: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Hessian Matrix & Convexity of Linear Regression Loss** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef calculus_hessian_convexity(X: list) -> dict:\n    arr = np.array(X, dtype=float)\n    H = (2.0 / arr.shape[0]) * (arr.T @ arr)\n    e = np.linalg.eigvalsh(H)\n    return {'hessian': np.round(H, 4).tolist(), 'eigenvalues': np.round(e, 4).tolist(), 'is_convex': bool(np.all(e >= -1e-9))}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
